.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH voa-verify 1  "voa-verify " 
.SH "نام (NAME)"
voa\-verify \- Verify a file using suitable verifiers and signatures.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBvoa verify\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR]... [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIOS\fR> <\fIPURPOSE\fR> <\fICONTEXT\fR> <\fITECHNOLOGY\fR> <\fIFILE\fR> [\fISIGNATURES\fR] 
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Verify a file using suitable verifiers and signatures.
.PP
Returns a status message on stdout.
.PP
Returns a non\-zero exit code and an error message on stderr, if the verification of one or more signature files fails.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
The output format to use.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json: The JSON output format
.IP \(bu 2
text: The default text output format
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBVOA_VERIFY_OUTPUT_FORMAT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase logging verbosity
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Decrease logging verbosity
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIOS\fR>
The OS to verify for.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBVOA_VERIFY_OS\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
<\fIPURPOSE\fR>
The purpose to verify for.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBVOA_VERIFY_PURPOSE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
<\fICONTEXT\fR>
The context to verify for.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBVOA_VERIFY_CONTEXT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
<\fITECHNOLOGY\fR>
The technology to verify with.

Currently only "openpgp" is supported.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBVOA_VERIFY_TECHNOLOGY\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The file to verify.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBVOA_VERIFY_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
[\fISIGNATURES\fR]
The signature to verify a file with.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBVOA_VERIFY_SIGNATURE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
